    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with significant leverage in the outfield, headlined by **James Wood** (77.71) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.90). **James Wood** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Ginn and elite xwOBA metrics that overcome a marginal threat from the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time. **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) are both prime candidates to capitalize on high-park-factor environments and favorable platoon splits against middling right-handed pitching. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) remains a locked-in asset at UTIL, as his plate discipline against Canning provides a high-floor profile that stabilizes our daily production.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Austin Riley** (52.82), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Austin Riley** carries significant power upside, his current efficiency profile against Gore\u2014coupled with a lower-order lineup spot\u2014fell just short of the high-ceiling production we expect from our middle-tier hitters like **Edwin Arroyo** (57.89). We are actively monitoring the status of **Jose Caballero**, who remains benched due to a confirmed rainout, while **Giancarlo Stanton** remains sidelined on the IL. Regarding risk management, **Corbin Carroll** (70.40) is worth watching closely; while his raw talent is elite, his score is slightly tempered by the defensive efficiency of the opposing battery, which suppresses his stolen base equity. We advise staying away from **Travis Bazzana** (33.76) today, as he falls well below our 40-point efficiency floor due to a brutal matchup against Montgomery.",
